# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces production before #4564 was fixed (#4600): a cross-shard
# migration import (MergeManyAsync with isCrossShardMigration) is dropped
# whenever the destination already holds a non-migrated row, whatever the
# stamps. Once the split's sweep has resolved a decided saga at the destination
# (a terminal write, so non-migrated), a later write accepted on the source is
# dropped by the shadow-forward and again by the final drain, so the map moves
# to a destination without it. The intended design merges the import
# last-writer-wins.
MODULE: NoKeyLostMigrationImportDropped
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a migration import over a non-migrated destination row is dropped, losing a later write across the split
PERTURBS: SplitCommit, LaterWrite

--- FIND
           into(x, s, k) == k = k2 /\ s = s2 /\ (x = c \/ (x = R /\ ResizeMirrors(c, s2)))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the import is dropped over a non-migrated destination row.
           into(x, s, k) == k = k2 /\ s = s2 /\ (x = c \/ (x = R /\ ResizeMirrors(c, s2)))
                            /\ ~(row[x][s][k] # Absent /\ ~mig[x][s][k])
--- END

--- FIND
                        IF k = k2 /\ <<x, y>> \in Landing(c, s, k2)
                        THEN LWW(row[x][y][k], WVal(c, s)) ELSE row[x][y][k]]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the split's shadow-forward is dropped over a non-migrated destination row.
                        IF k = k2 /\ <<x, y>> \in Landing(c, s, k2)
                           /\ ~(<<x, y>> # <<c, s>> /\ y = s2 /\ SplitMirrors(x, s1, k2)
                                /\ row[x][y][k] # Absent /\ ~mig[x][y][k])
                        THEN LWW(row[x][y][k], WVal(c, s)) ELSE row[x][y][k]]]]
--- END